Z||000000||Black86SE||11-06-2001||01:51 PM||||Okay, I am changing my car from an auto to a isuzu 5-speed and I am wondering which Clutch Master Cylinder to use. The tranny is out of an '88 and didn't know if I had to use one specific to the tranny or year of my car (an '86). Plus, which one is considered the "cast" and which one is the "tube" style? Also, does anybody know the part numbers for these? <BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Black 1986 V6 SE<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS<BR>AIM ScreenName: Black86se||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-06-2001||02:55 PM||||I would use the newer "tube" style master, but it sort of depends on which hydraulic line you will be using.  The early Fieros that used the cast master have different hydraulic lines (different bends, etc.) than the later ones with the tube style, so it would be difficult to attach this line to the newer style.  It may be possible to persuade it on, but be prepared for problems (just in case).<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
